        "original_id": "34658371-5d52-55e7-9064-c29cd12d667f",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Summerseat, Greater Manchester, England, north west England, Heywood, Rawtenstall, Bury Bolton Street, Burrs Country Park, Ramsbottom, Irwell Vale, Broadfield\n- Organizations: East Lancashire Railway\n- Systems: Summerseat railway station, Broadfield railway station, heritage railway lines\n\nFacts:\n- Summerseat railway station is a preserved railway station that serves the village of Summerseat in Greater Manchester, England.\n- Summerseat railway station is part of the heritage East Lancashire Railway.\n- The East Lancashire Railway is a heritage railway line in north west England that runs between Heywood and Rawtenstall.\n- The East Lancashire Railway is about 12 to 12.5 miles long.\n- The East Lancashire Railway has intermediate stations at Bury Bolton Street, Burrs Country Park, Summerseat, Ramsbottom, and Irwell Vale.\n- The line through Broadfield railway station has been reopened by the heritage East Lancashire Railway.\n- Broadfield railway station itself remains disused.",
